839c920219073a5dc44b971aa365e98f5e7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788455883, "git_changesets": ["6d52fbee9ce42eb5285fe327f448b4ad69ff6fb0"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "28342": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chris Martin \u003cmarti4d@live.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068333 - Restore minidump-writer behavior of ignoring fpregs errors  a=dmeehan\n\nIn Isolated Processes #2, I accidentally changed the behavior of floating-\npoint register reading to return a hard error on failure instead of ignoring\nthe error and simply returning the default value.\n\nThis has blocked all minidump generation on ARM on older Linux Kernels that\ndon't support the new PTRACE_GETREGSET APIs.\n\nThis hotfix simply restores the previous behavior.\n\nLink to bug-introducing diff: https://github.com/rust-minidump/minidump-writer/pull/175/changes#diff-a3ec3f7ac451b5fb1ad7c5f5f28898d16b06d36c94936bcbf5257180edb3b37cL60\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323003\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323240\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "third_party/rust/minidump-writer/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/minidump-writer/src/linux/thread_info/arm.rs", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_client/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_server/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/crashreporter/rust_minidump_writer_linux/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": "5678bb1a01e5203508e3b458639e015519c88d2d", "git_parents": ["6d52fbee9ce42eb5285fe327f448b4ad69ff6fb0"], "node": "1fbf24341ee3673b3740da54f09547aad996cd8d", "parents": ["02a7c2ab0e93df2fc47352ac0286742b4c6f6c37"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788456708, "git_changesets": ["5678bb1a01e5203508e3b458639e015519c88d2d"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "28343": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067586 - Properly annotate proxyFilter channel with isTRRServiceChannel  a=dmeehan\n\nProxyConfigLookup synthesizes a throwaway nsHttpChannel for the proxy filter check\nand that didn't properly match the isTRRServiceChannel flag of the real TRR channel.\nThis patch makes sure the flag is correctly passed to the filter.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322858\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323179\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/TRRServiceBase.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/PSocketProcess.ipdl", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookup.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookup.h", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookupChild.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookupChild.h", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookupParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/ProxyConfigLookupParent.h", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/TRRServiceChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_trr_proxy_channel_filter.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "c9119ff0e3ce2af308bf7681c5cced7dfa75d063", "git_parents": ["5678bb1a01e5203508e3b458639e015519c88d2d"], "node": "61d0f7f87d9800652df9c962094d778a3080ed68", "parents": ["1fbf24341ee3673b3740da54f09547aad996cd8d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788457761, "git_changesets": ["c9119ff0e3ce2af308bf7681c5cced7dfa75d063"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "28344": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067531: Add two Windows App SDK DLLs to the Firefox packager  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322798\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323271\n", "files": ["browser/installer/package-manifest.in", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-WindowsAppSDK.sh", "toolkit/content/license.html", "widget/windows/moz.build"], "git_node": "7c6dbcce259a60c01f730ae31275622b46faddcc", "git_parents": ["c9119ff0e3ce2af308bf7681c5cced7dfa75d063"], "node": "ffaa8738a48511f8c46d38fee66dd21c48641238", "parents": ["61d0f7f87d9800652df9c962094d778a3080ed68"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788457924, "git_changesets": ["7c6dbcce259a60c01f730ae31275622b46faddcc"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "28345": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068308 - Disable LoadRemainderRGB_SIMD neon/neon64 specialization on neon.  a=dmeehan\n\nThere are alignment issues on neon for arm32 only devices. This is\nthe safest fix to land for now and we can finetune the performance\nanother day.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323253\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323294\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/SwizzleNEON.h"], "git_node": "c7f3300472025da72fc82a5f35bdb35de2ef4aa2", "git_parents": ["7c6dbcce259a60c01f730ae31275622b46faddcc"], "node": "74f71d5d4b6dff69410f04ee9fb10e7bb6d17e2d", "parents": ["ffaa8738a48511f8c46d38fee66dd21c48641238"], "tags": []}], "date": 1788461870, "git_changesets": ["c7f3300472025da72fc82a5f35bdb35de2ef4aa2"], "user": "dmeehan@mozilla.com"}, "28346": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055858 - Honor the wallpaper visible and visibility_group fields in the New Tab picker  a=dmeehan\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323031\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323344\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.test.jsx"], "git_node": "cd7d1d5e32180e2782d659d70b90dfe6fdd149aa", "git_parents": ["c7f3300472025da72fc82a5f35bdb35de2ef4aa2"], "node": "2c983f8e2ebbd4a9670675b6cca92eac892ae09c", "parents": ["74f71d5d4b6dff69410f04ee9fb10e7bb6d17e2d"], "tag